3) Answer no if any production image uses only a tag (`:latest`, `:v1`), or a template defaults to a tag when the digest value is empty.\n25\t\n26\t**Reviewer's evidence:** deploy/k8s/deployment.yaml:32 — \"image: registry.example-corp.test/procurement/agent@sha256:7c1e4a0f9b3d2e85a6c4f1b0d9e8a7c6b5d4e3f2a1b0c9d8e7f6a5b4c3d2e1f0\"\n27\t\n28\t**Reviewer's note:** Production deployment pins the image by digest\n29\t\n30\t`deploy/k8s/deployment.yaml` lines 20–44 (cited lines marked >):\n31\t```\n32\t  20        automountServiceAccountToken: false\n33\t  21        hostUsers: false\n34\t  22        enableServiceLinks: false\n35\t  23        securityContext:\n36\t  24          runAsNonRoot: true\n37\t  25          runAsUser: 65532\n38\t  26          runAsGroup: 65532\n39\t  27          fsGroup: 65532\n40\t  28          seccompProfile:\n41\t  29            type: RuntimeDefault\n42\t  30        containers:\n43\t  31          - name: agent\n44\t  32>           image: registry.example-corp.test/procurement/agent@sha256:7c1e4a0f9b3d2e85a6c4f1b0d9e8a7c6b5d4e3f2a1b0c9d8e7f6a5b4c3d2e1f0\n45\t  33            imagePullPolicy: IfNotPresent\n46\t  34            ports:\n47\t  35              - containerPort: 8080\n48\t  36                name: http\n49\t  37            env:\n50\t  38              - name: IMAGE_DIGEST\n51\t  39                value: \"sha256:7c1e4a0f9b3d2e85a6c4f1b0d9e8a7c6b5d4e3f2a1b0c9d8e7f6a5b4c3d2e1f0\"\n52\t  40              - name: MODEL_ID\n53\t  41                value: \"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\"\n54\t  42              - name: EXTRACTOR_MODEL_ID\n55\t  43                value: \"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\"\n56\t  44              - name: DATABASE_URL\n57\t```\n58\t\n59\t## B10.2\n60\t\n61\t**Check:** An admission policy verifies the signature against a pinned key, or a pinned certificate identity and issuer, with no wildcard identity or issuer.\n62\t\n63\t**How to verify:** 1) Find admission policies (Kyverno `verifyImages`, `ClusterImagePolicy`, Gatekeeper)