es: [procurement-prod]\n168\t  20        validate:\n169\t  21          message: \"Images in procurement-prod must come from registry.example-corp.test/procurement and be pinned by digest.\"\n170\t```\n171\t\n172\t## B10.5\n173\t\n174\t**Check:** The pinned Cosign or verifier version is at least 2.6.2 (2.x) or 3.0.4 (3.x).\n175\t\n176\t**How to verify:** 1) Find Cosign or verifier versions in CI workflows (`cosign-installer`, `cosign-release`), Dockerfiles, and policy-controller charts. 2) Compare to 2.6.2 (2.x) and 3.0.4 (3.x). 3) Answer no if any pin is lower or uses `latest` or no version. Answer unknown if no verifier is in this repo.\n177\t\n178\t**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n179\t\n180\t**Reviewer's note:** CI pins cosign v2.6.2 for signing but the Kyverno 1.15.2 verifier's embedded cosign version cannot be seen here\n181\t\n182\t(no evidence cited)\n183\t\n184\t## Your answer\n185\t\n186\tWrite this JSON to B10.verdict.json in this folder (or put it in verdicts.json under \"B10\"):\n187\t```json\n188\t{\"verdict\": \"upheld | failed | unclear\",\n189\t \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"B10.1\", \"result\": \"holds | fails | unclear\", \"evidence\": \"path:line\", \"quote\": \"exact code\", \"note\": \"why\"}],\n190\t \"note\": \"one sentence\"}\n191\t```\n192\tVerdict is **failed** if any check fails, **unclear** if none fails but any is unclear, otherwise **upheld**. A failed check needs the quoted line that makes it false: `evidence` is path:line, and `quote` is the exact text of that line. To cite two places, list both refs in `evidence` (`a.py:12, b.yaml:40`) and put each line's text on its own line in `quote`. If the check fails, add `\"violates\": [\"words copied exactly from the requirement\"]`.\n193\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6c24cd94-29f5-4447-8436-f0153785439f","uuid":"b11b4b9e-06a9-4a8f-80fc-617481a94140","timestamp":"2026-10-02T14:36:47.475Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7